00:36:29.645 --> 00:36:32.023
Best way to convey the contrast

00:36:32.023 --> 00:36:35.234
between the favelas
and these informal housing.

00:36:35.735 --> 00:36:36.944
And Elysium.

00:36:36.944 --> 00:36:40.198
Here is that there's

00:36:40.198 --> 00:36:43.159
no wall between the dining room
and the toilet.

00:36:43.993 --> 00:36:45.536
And yeah.

00:36:45.536 --> 00:36:48.372
So if you have guests over for dinner
and you have to pee,

00:36:49.415 --> 00:36:52.627
well, you're out of luck.

00:36:52.627 --> 00:36:55.588
I think the first luxury that goes
when you're live in poverty

00:36:55.588 --> 00:36:58.090
is probably privacy.

00:36:58.090 --> 00:37:02.595
And I think this space, this apartment
actually creates a pretty strong

00:37:02.595 --> 00:37:06.390
narrative of what's happening because it's
actually a pretty large space.

00:37:06.390 --> 00:37:11.354
It's probably somewhere around like 400
square feet, but it's not well-designed.

00:37:11.520 --> 00:37:16.776
It was just put together out of necessity
because someone needed space ASAP.

00:37:16.943 --> 00:37:20.571
Yeah, it tells a story of a city
and a population that's been abandoned.

00:37:20.613 --> 00:37:23.032
You know, there's like no building codes
saying

00:37:23.324 --> 00:37:26.786
there needs to be a wall
between the toilet and the dining room.

00:37:26.786 --> 00:37:30.748
And there's, like,
no jurisdiction cracking down on the

00:37:30.748 --> 00:37:34.627
basic spatial constraints.

00:37:36.212 --> 00:37:36.671
I like how

00:37:36.671 --> 00:37:40.424
even in the future for the mega,
mega rich,

00:37:40.716 --> 00:37:44.595
they still have like very conventional
looking

00:37:45.263 --> 00:37:47.765
kind of Victorian style houses,

00:37:47.765 --> 00:44:52.022
but with circles, circular windows.

00:44:53.023 --> 00:44:56.276
So the entire movie takes place
in one building in this

00:44:56.694 --> 00:45:00.698
this house of the CEO and the upstairs.

00:45:00.739 --> 00:45:02.783
You have views everywhere.

00:45:02.783 --> 00:45:07.830
And I think it's just so fascinating
how just by using these two floors

00:45:08.080 --> 00:45:11.166
and using glass, it's able to create

00:45:11.166 --> 00:45:14.461
so many different scenarios

00:45:43.699 --> 00:45:45.576
with a little skylight.

00:45:45.576 --> 00:45:48.704
But that's pretty much
your only connection to nature.

00:45:48.787 --> 00:45:51.665
The basement is where the A.I.,

00:45:51.707 --> 00:45:54.835
the Android
and the test subject are living.

00:45:54.835 --> 00:45:58.088
So it's a pretty big contrast
and it creates these

00:45:58.088 --> 00:46:18.734
two worlds.

00:46:19.443 --> 00:46:21.779
It's floor to ceiling glass.

00:46:21.779 --> 00:46:26.742
You can see the mountains and the trees
and the downstairs basement.

00:46:27.493 --> 00:46:29.536
There's no windows.

00:46:29.536 --> 00:46:32.915
There's this little garden with

00:46:32.915 --> 00:48:24.443
these trees.

00:48:25.986 --> 00:48:26.945
I think this lens

00:48:26.945 --> 00:48:29.948
flare here is pretty intentional.

00:48:30.824 --> 00:48:36.079
And you can see that in a lot of
the scenes that's taking place upstairs.

00:48:36.079 --> 00:48:38.498
There's a lot
of like lens flare and light.

